        "description": "**Status:** implemented\n\n**Contract(s):** scanner callback with stable sourceResultId, active scanAttemptId, verdict, scanner identity, exact byte count, sealed-object ETag/key, SHA-256, timestamp, and bounded details\n\n**AuthZ:** system-admin (admin/security_admin) bearer auth or configured server-to-server scanner token; club admins are denied; scanner callbacks must own the active unexpired attempt; matching result retries return 200, conflicting/stale retries return 409; manual admins cannot declare CLEAN; scanner CLEAN requires the deterministic server-only sealed key; INFECTED, MIME/magic mismatch, permanent size/limit failures, exhausted callbacks, and expired/crashed attempts at the configured ceiling terminate unavailable\n\n**UI anchors:** the supervised worker advertises a short database heartbeat, reclaims expired scan leases, verifies definition freshness plus clean/EICAR probes, validates declared MIME against magic bytes, scans real Supabase private objects, seals clean bytes, and reports verdicts; staging cleanup starts only after signed-URL expiry plus the configured grace period and retries with audit diagnostics\n\n**Source:** `docs/backend-api/ROUTE_INVENTORY_V1.md`",
